{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggzCm7Y1EZCpBZQUsbCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CNtrYP8NNxjDEy8r5tWLkS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x5c5240-research/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"mouseGround\\|new E.View\\|E.VIEWS\\|screenDirToGround\\|groundDirToScreen\\|view.p(\" API-INDEX.md | head -12; sed -n 1017,1037p API-INDEX.md","description":"Look up views, mouse-to-ground and the Bullets API"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":247431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17","uuid":"a613e2c1-714e-4dba-83ed-1fe2b9d06d9c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:03:19.354Z","request_id":"req_011CggzCkpBEuQEqMi3DA7xD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CNtrYP8NNxjDEy8r5tWLkS":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/x5c5240-research/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"mouseGround\\|new E.View\\|E.VIEWS\\|screenDirToGround\\|groundDirToScreen\\|view.p(\" API-INDEX.md | head -12; sed -n 1017,1037p API-INDEX.md","description":"Look up views, mouse-to-ground and the Bullets API"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNtrYP8NNxjDEy8r5tWLkS","type":"tool_result","content":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n## 18. Bullets\n\n- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n- `E.pattern`: velocity helpers for bullet patterns. Angles in radians (0 = east / right). Each returns [vx, v2] or a list of them\n- `E.pattern.aim(a, b, speed)`: aim from a to b on the ground plane (x, y); aimSide uses x, z\n- `E.pattern.aimSide(a, b, speed)`: a velocity from a toward b in a side view (x, z)\n- `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`: one velocity at an angle\n- `E.pattern.ring(n, speed, offset = 0)`: n bullets in a full circle, rotated by offset\n- `E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`: n bullets fanned across `arc` radians around `angle`\n\n## 19. Spatial hash\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17","uuid":"3e071a05-2393-4d2d-af68-0af72a67de78","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:03:19.375Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n## 18. Bullets\n\n- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n- `E.pattern`: velocity helpers for bullet patterns. Angles in radians (0 = east / right). Each returns [vx, v2] or a list of them\n- `E.pattern.aim(a, b, speed)`: aim from a to b on the ground plane (x, y); aimSide uses x, z\n- `E.pattern.aimSide(a, b, speed)`: a velocity from a toward b in a side view (x, z)\n- `E.pattern.dir(angle, speed)`: one velocity at an angle\n- `E.pattern.ring(n, speed, offset = 0)`: n bullets in a full circle, rotated by offset\n- `E.pattern.spread(angle, n, arc, speed)`: n bullets fanned across `arc` radians around `angle`\n\n## 19. Spatial hash","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CNtrYP8NNxjDEy8r5tWLkS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
